{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Who establishes</b> — Because he mentioned the earth, he mentioned the mountains because they are like pillars." "<b>And the meaning of \"girded with might\"</b> — that the might of HaShem was seen in the high mountains He created; therefore they are called \"mountains of El.\" And in my opinion: he mentioned that He is the assurance of the thing that is not seen, and His might is seen in the great bodies."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 65, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:43.668142487Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}